Nina R: Heads up - I can reliably repro a 3-6 char replay at the start of resumed SSE payloads in our browser polyfill when tokens rotate. Happens in Chrome and embedded webviews.

Omar G: Polyfill only? Native EventSource behaves?

Nina R: Native is clean. Polyfill parse state appears to be the culprit. Repro: open stream -> short-lived token refresh -> SDK reconnects -> resumed event begins with tail of previous chunk then continues.

Lee S: Likely buffer + inclusive resume overlap. Do you still keep an in-memory partial buffer across reconnects?

Nina R: Yup, simplified loop:
```
let buf = '';
polyfill.ondata = chunk => {
  buf += chunk;
  const evts = buf.split('\n\n');
  buf = evts.pop() || '';
  for (const e of evts) emitEvent(e);
};
// reconnect currently preserves buf
```

Omar G: Two quick mitigations: clear buf on reconnect; and prefer server-side exclusive resume offsets. Also add lightweight dedupe by seq id on the client to ignore overlap.

ops-bot: note - staging nginx has proxy_read_timeout=60s causing mid-chunk closes under load.

Nina R: I'll open a small PR that clears the parse buffer on reconnect, exposes resumeMode: \"exclusive\"|\"inclusive\" (default exclusive), and adds a unit test simulating a mid-chunk TCP close.

Lee S: Add server keepalive heartbeat recommendation (":hb\n\n" every 20s) so proxies don't close idle conns. Ensure heartbeats are ignored and not billed. Also spec that SDKs accept both Last-Event-ID header and resume_token query param for parity.

Omar G: Short-term fallback: if resume fails >3 times, switch to short-polling to avoid UX duplicates.

ci-bot: CI started for branch fix/sse-polyfill-resume (build 9124) :rocket:

Nina R: Action items:
- Nina: PR to clear buffer on reconnect + tests
- Omar: spec for header parity + client dedupe by seq
- Ops: nginx example and heartbeat guidance

Nina R: Will tag reviewers and attach repro traces. Closing once CI green. :white_check_mark:
